Forty Points epilogue: open problem 6 (Numbers) brought up to date with Passes 12004-12050 (Claude track, no new claims)

Replaces the stale 'strong-CP problem of the chain is open ... twelve parameters' wording with the established state:
- the Weber law (elliptic homes miss; CM points do not but running blocks identification, 12046);
- Nelson-Barr necessity and sufficiency (12004/12005/12044);
- the geometric row fits quarks but not leptons at any scale (12045-12047);
- canonical potentials repel the hierarchy and neither Wilson lines nor fluxes give eps ~ 1/150 naturally (12048, 12050);
- the conditional SU(5) threshold with one vectorlike pair (12049).
The sharpened question: what keeps eps small?

